365:The last chapter — the ledger, the file, and the door into Arc 3, in the series' Chapter 24 register: small leavings and stayings, each heavier than its size. The first true edge-territories camp: a switchback shelf above an unnamed valley, firelight, the found family's roles running on new terrain with old grammar — Brom's quiet competence now aimed at load-balancing a cart instead of acquiring dinner twice over; Karis indexing her three boxes into a working field-archive; Lira mapping tomorrow's route like a bracket sheet; Seln gone for an hour and back with the lay of every approach, unasked; Ephram's absence at the fire noted once, without grief — he stayed, and staying was right for him, and the family's arithmetic holds him anyway. The ledger of the year, in its established forms. The Power Log inventory, in Hesk's satchel, by firelight, shown complete: **nine confirmed fragments** — Wind-adjacent (Lira), Pressure-adjacent (Feryn), Iron-adjacent (Brom), Compression-adjacent (Reydan), Ember-adjacent (Karis), Shadow-adjacent (Seln), Storm-adjacent (Daeva), Anchor-adjacent (unnamed), Blade-adjacent (Ephram) — nine integrated abilities, each with a name beside it except the one the system sent namelessly, and the anomaly, session nine, Tide-adjacent, turned over once, closed with the standing three words: *Still open. Still real. Patience.* One log line for the old promises: "Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. The road east is long. Good." Letters, held for the next westbound courier whenever one exists: to Hesk (*"Eighteen, unenrolled, and past the Line. The shape you said to mind — I minded it. The tools fit the road. — C."*), to Vell, because her ledger holds his first honest record and the resignation belongs in it.
