369:The last lines, matched to the series' pattern: "I have nine things that aren't a Path," Cael said, eventually, to nobody in particular, "no tier, no rank, no enrollment, no protection — and five people who signed out of the world that was supposed to provide them." He turned it over once and let it stand. "And somewhere behind us, a file with a new sentence in it, written by nobody, same as always." Lira, feeding the fire: "Let them escalate. They'll need better maps." Brom: "And better roads." Karis, writing: "Noted." Down the fire, the man who used to file reports about him watched the dark east horizon with evident professional approval and said nothing, which — from him — was home.
370-
371-The hand had signed its last instrument with his name on it. He wasn't inside its jurisdiction anymore. The fire burned in a territory no Arbiter had ever measured — and for the first time in seven years, nothing anywhere was deciding what he was, except him.
